meta {
  name: 01 Happy path
  seq: 1
}

docs {
  # GET /users/{userId}/personal-records

  A client's personal records for one exercise, all-time or within an inclusive date range.

  | Query | Rules |
  |-------|-------|
  | `exerciseName` | **required**, catalog name (trimmed, case-insensitive) |
  | `unit` | `kg` (default) or `lb` |
  | `from`, `to` | optional inclusive `YYYY-MM-DD` bounds; `from <= to` |

  Metrics, each taken from the single best set (they may come from different sets):

  - `maxWeight` – heaviest set weight
  - `maxVolume` – highest `reps × weight` in one set
  - `bestE1rm` – highest Epley estimate `weight × (1 + reps / 30)`

  Each record is `{ value, weight, reps, date, entryId }` or `null` without data. `date` is the day the record
  was **first** reached. Values are rounded to 2 decimals; a weight shown in the unit it was logged in is exact.

  ```json
  {
    "data": {
      "exerciseName": "Bench Press", "unit": "kg", "from": null, "to": null,
      "records": {
        "maxWeight": { "value": 112.5, "weight": 112.5, "reps": 3, "date": "2026-10-06", "entryId": "…" },
        "maxVolume": { "value": 760, "weight": 95, "reps": 8, "date": "2026-10-06", "entryId": "…" },
        "bestE1rm": { "value": 123.75, "weight": 112.5, "reps": 3, "date": "2026-10-06", "entryId": "…" }
      }
    }
  }
  ```

  `message` is added when every record is `null`.
}
